hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21587","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, I heard Abu Ishaq, that he heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir narrating from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Subh, and said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: These two prayers are among the heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites. Had they known what is in them, they would come to them even crawling. And the front row is like the row of the angels. Had you known its merit, you would hasten to it. And a man's prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with one man. And the more, the more beloved to Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"21588","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Fajr. When he prayed, he said: Is so-and-so present? The people were silent. They said: Yes, and he had not attended. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The heaviest prayer upon the hypocrites is 'Isha and Fajr. Had they known what is in them, they would come to them even crawling. And the first row is like the row of the angels. Had you known its merit, you would hasten to it. Your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with one man. And your prayer with one man is purer than your prayer alone. And the more, the more beloved to Allah, Exalted. My father said: Waki' said: 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir al-'Anami."
"21589","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from his father, he said: Abu Ishaq said: And I heard it from him and from his father. He said: I heard Ubayy ibn Ka'b say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the Subh prayer one day, and he mentioned the hadith."
"21590","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Abu 'Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid, meaning ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the hadith."
"21591","Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from his father, he said: I came to Madinah and met Ubayy ibn Ka'b. I said: Abu al-Mundhir, narrate to me the most amazing hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us, or for us, the morning prayer. Then he turned to us with his face and said: Is so-and-so present? And he mentioned the hadith."
"21592","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Abdullah, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from his father, he said: I came to Madinah and met Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and he mentioned the like of that."
"21593","Abdullah narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Basir al-'Abdi, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the morning prayer, then said: Is so-and-so present? And he mentioned the hadith."
"21594","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had people known what is in 'Isha and the morning prayer of merit in congregation, they would come to them even crawling."
"21595","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-'Ayizar ibn Hurayth, from Abu Basir, he said: Ubayy said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us the Fajr prayer. When he finished prayer, he saw fewness among the people of the mosque. He said: Is so-and-so present? We said: Yes, until he counted three men. He said: No prayer is heavier upon the hypocrites than the last 'Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer. And he mentioned the hadith at length."
"21596","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Hubab al-Quta'i narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from a man of 'Abd al-Qays, from Ubayy, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with us the Subh prayer. When he finished his prayer, he turned to us with his face, then said: The heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites are these two prayers."
